### Ledger Service - REST API Routes

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. POST - Create a new ledger transaction
### Description: Posts a balanced ledger transaction with double-entry accounting
### Rules:
###   - Entries must be balanced (sum of amounts = 0)
###   - All entries must use the same currency
###   - Returns 204 No Content on success
POST {{baseUrl}}/ledger/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Transfer from Account A to Account B",
  "externalReference": "EXT-REF-001",
  "entries": [
    {
      "accountId": "acct-client-001",
      "amount": -10000,
      "currency": "USD"
    },
    {
      "accountId": "acct-pending-settlement",
      "amount": 10000,
      "currency": "USD"
    }
  ]
}

### 2. GET - List all ledger transactions
### Description: Retrieves all saved transactions with their entries
### Returns: Array of transactions (empty array if none exist)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ledger/transactions
